# Normalise line endings.
#
# Without this, files committed from Windows carry CRLF into the repository,
# and the Linux host we deploy to (Phase 14) sees them in shell scripts and
# config. Worse, every checkout on a different OS shows the whole file as
# modified, which makes diffs and blame useless.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` stores LF in the repository and checks out LF everywhere,
# including Windows. Modern Windows tooling handles LF fine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be line-ending converted -- doing so corrupts them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
